.TH "CSDLC-CLEAN" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-clean \- preview and remove an eligible registered worktree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc clean ISSUE
\&csdlc clean ISSUE \-\-execute \-\-preview TOKEN
\&csdlc clean \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json
\&csdlc clean \-\-help
.fi
.SH ISSUE INTENT FORM
\&The semantic issue intent form is the current operational interface. It resolves issue identity and routes effects through the native semantic transaction owner.
.PP
\&The intent preview returns preview_token on stdout without a token file. Execution compares the issue generation/digest, authority, exact target/head, terminal receipt, topology, policy and native preview before the owner repeats cleanup admission. Dirty/live/stale targets remain refused. Retained terminal evidence plus no registered issue binding can establish an observational repeated\-clean no\-op, never permission to remove another checkout.
.PP
\&Optional \-\-repo\-root selects discovery, \-\-json retains machine output, and \-\-emit\-request returns a generated wrapper accepted directly by COMMAND \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json; its inner request is also accepted. Both forms share identity and mutation guards.
.PP
\&The candidate intent cleanup bridge archives only exact generated untracked issue cards/evidence/completed transaction records and lock after admission, verifies durable copied bytes/permissions/symlink text, then removes originals with the index last. Tracked changes and unrelated untracked bytes remain refused. Retained request\-based cleanup remains unchanged. After interrupted removal, obtain a fresh clean preview and explicitly continue cleanup. Verified archived index evidence can authorize only cleanup continuation; it does not restore implementation authority.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&Requires durable terminal receipt identity and digest, actual registered candidate, approved parent, exact matching head and clean non\-live checkout. First use cleanup.remove false; inspect Removable and save returned receipt_digest. Then use remove true with that preview_receipt_digest and unchanged target identity. Removal is separate from finish. Dirty/live/unregistered/protected paths are not permission to delete manually.
.SH OPTIONS
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&\-\-request: Required path to a UTF\-8 JSON request of the command's request family.
.PP
\&\-\-help: Show standalone help; \-h is equivalent.
.PP
\&\-h: Show standalone help; do not combine with execution options.
.PP
\&\-\-intent\-request: Execute an exact generated csdlc.v3.intent_request.v1 request or its generated wrapper; stale snapshots fail closed.
.SH REQUEST
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&TerminalRouteRequest, with only the relevant finish, cleanup or cutover fields. See csdlc\-requests(1). Examples under docs/csdlc\-v3/man/examples use fixture identities and are not permission to mutate those targets.
.SH EFFECTS
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&Preview inspects; remove true may remove exactly the registered candidate after repeated guards. It does not authorize broad branch/worktree cleanup.
.SH FILES
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&Primary terminal paths: resolved Git metadata csdlc\-v3/local/v3/issues/ISSUE/terminal.json and csdlc\-v3/local/evidence/ISSUE/terminal\-receipt.json. Linked paths: .csdlc/v3/issues/ISSUE/terminal.json and .csdlc/evidence/ISSUE/terminal\-receipt.json. Request terminal_state.repository_root must be the real reconciliation checkout; state_path and receipt_path must resolve exactly to those locations.
.SH EXAMPLES
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.nf
\&csdlc clean 870
\&csdlc clean 870 \-\-execute \-\-preview TOKEN
.fi
.PP
\&Use csdlc\-workflow(1) for ordered finish and cleanup; cutover/rollback examples validate the schema and denial boundary, not a new transition authorization.
.SH RECOVERY
\&The legacy \-\-request writer syntax is retired. It remains visible only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery; execution fails before request parsing or effects. The semantic issue form above is the current operational interface.
.PP
\&Retain original evidence and exact current checkout identity. Stale terminal state requires a matching expected_state_digest; mismatched receipt identity must be investigated, never overwritten. Refresh a clean preview after any target/head/registration change. Unsupported or unproven transition states fail closed; do not fall back to deleted wrappers.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1), csdlc\-workflow(1).
